
Implemented centralized security controls across the Windows 11 workstation environment using Group Policy. Created and linked a GPO_Workstation_Security policy to the Workstations OU, allowing security configurations to be centrally managed and automatically applied to CLIENT01. 
Configured password and account lockout policies to strengthen authentication and reduce the risk of brute-force attacks, enabled Windows Defender Firewall with inbound connections blocked by default and outbound connections allowed, and configured advanced security auditing to generate useful authentication, account-management, and system activity logs. 
Verified that the GPO was successfully applied to CLIENT01 using gpupdate /force and gpresult, and validated the firewall configuration through command-line tools.
This phase established a centralized workstation-hardening baseline and laid the foundation for the endpoint monitoring and SIEM integration performed in Phase 4.
